     "tests_reduce_only_clamp": "that the venue always CLAMPS a reduceOnly order that exceeds the position rather than refusing it — observed on 2026-09-12 12Z (MEMEUSDT/POPCATUSDT, origQty = the position to the contract, no error) and documented, assumed general; and that the allOrders record of a clamped request has the shape this suite rebuilds from the submit response + the child fills (the live record was not logged). It proves, against the real gates (`submit_identity_mismatch`, `last_fill_details`, `venue_fills.settle_ambiguous_legs`) driven by the REAL 12Z submit responses and the REAL 08Z/12Z readbacks, that a reduceOnly record whose origQty is BELOW ours is the fourth state `clamped` (recorded, orig_qty = the position, no `inconsistent`), that an origQty ABOVE ours, a non-reduceOnly difference and a wrong side are still contradictions at every gate (the 1e-6 tolerance is untouched), that `plan()` sizes a full exit as −held_qty from the same account snapshot (F2 removed at the source; no quantity ⇒ the old path, labelled `notional_over_mid`), and end to end through the unmodified plan→submit_maker→complete_anchor chain over a scripted transport that the maker rows close on the venue's capacity (`qty_venue`) and `reconcile` measures both names at residual 0 where the old code produced 2 × execution_of_unknown_size (the incident, reproduced from the live rows as a control; the origQty-above-ours mutation of the same chain still produces the 2 anomalies). It does NOT run the watchdog (the proportional response is (c), a separate ruling), nor prove that mark ≠ mid is the ONLY way ours can exceed the position.",
     "tests_flatten_fee_backfill": "that the venue's allOrders still lists the flatten's orders when the runner is invoked (limit 500 / startTime — an unreached symbol is named, not fabricated), or that the LIVE run was ever performed (`LIVE_MODE=LIVE python3 ops/backfill_fills.py --day 20260912 --apply` is the operator's step, with credentials; this suite drives the runner over an in-process fake). It proves, on the REAL 2026-09-12 day, that the flatten batch is detected as the one gap with its 255 own client ids and 255 fee-unmeasured order rows, and on a synthetic population that the legs are rebuilt by EXACT client id (never by the rebalance-id prefix a flatten does not carry), that --apply writes one fills row per child fill with order_type protective_flatten and the venue's commission, that a second apply writes nothing (idempotent by trade id), that a foreign trade is counted unattributed and never written, that a batch the venue does not list fails closed, and that the classic rebalance path and its maker/topup_taker buckets are untouched. The ORDER rows' fee_paid stays None by the ledger's append-only rule — the measurement lands on the fills rows, and a consumer that sums fees from order rows alone still under-reads the flatten.",
+    "tests_proportional_response": "that 2% of gross and 5 names are the right lines (policy set after the 09-12 incident, frozen by R-14), that the venue behaves for reduce-only market exits during -4400 or price protection as it does in MockBroker, that the off-box page is DELIVERED (run_anchor's call is pinned statically; delivery is the anchor's receipt), and that ops/resume_from_trip.sh and ops/unseed_rehearsal_halt.py refuse end to end (both run a public network probe; their refusal branches are pinned statically and the EMA keep/remove snippet is executed verbatim). It proves, through watchdog.run on a held 100-name MockBroker book and on the real 2026-09-12 12Z rows re-shaped so (a)(b) keeps the contradiction, that a name-scoped trigger set (§4-5b, §4-5e split_unauth per-name clause alone, §4-7 drift) of <= 5 names whose doubt is <= 2% of the anchors row's target gross gets a LOCAL response — opening halted, resting orders cancelled and the WHOLE venue position flattened reduce-only for THOSE names only, the reduce-only key not set, state kind proportional_local — at 4/5/6 names and 1,999/2,000/2,001 USDT of 100,000, across the §4-5b/§4-5e union; that any book-level trigger beside it (§4-2, §4-5a) and the negative controls alone (§4-2, §4-4b, §4-5a, §4-5c) still flatten every name; that an unknown doubt or gross is named and never becomes a book-level flatten on its own while a KNOWN part over 2% still does; that a trigger nobody scoped is book-level; that the doubt of a name is a sum over every leg of unknown size (review C9: row order cannot change the route); that a local response never overwrites a standing trip's record and does not reset the harvest EMA; that the config switch false restores the ladder and an unreadable config reads ON; that unreadable positions across the book never reached the ladder before this change and still do not; and that the 2026-09-09 receipt's name sets (9 + 52) stay on the ladder.",
